{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-01-Jul-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The age of the older of two boys is thrice that of the younger. 9 years ago it was five times that of the younger. Find the present age of each.", "options": [{"text": "15 years, 45 years", "added": false}, {"text": "12 years, 36 years", "added": false}, {"text": "17 years, 51 years", "added": false}, {"text": "18 years, 54 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The respective ratio between numerical values of the curved surface area and the volume of a right circular cylinder is 2 : 3. If the respective ratio between the radius and the height of the cylinder is 3 : 7, what is the total surface area of the cylinder?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Find the number when successively divided by 3,5and 7 leaves remainder 2,1and 3, respectively, and the last quotient is 3.", "options": [{"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "362", "added": false}, {"text": "365", "added": false}, {"text": "367", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "In a circle, ABCD is a cyclic quadrilateral in which AE is drawn parallel to CD, and BA is produced to F. If ∠ ABC = 85° and ∠ FAE = 24°, find the value of ∠ BCD.", "options": [{"text": "125°", "added": false}, {"text": "115°", "added": false}, {"text": "124°", "added": false}, {"text": "119°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "cyclic-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "If 18 toys out of 75 toys are for boys and the rest are for girls, what is the percentage of girls toys?", "options": [{"text": "18%", "added": false}, {"text": "57%", "added": false}, {"text": "67%", "added": false}, {"text": "76%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A person drives 110 miles at 55 miles per hour, he drives the next 120 miles at 60 miles per hour, and then he drives the next 60 miles in an hour. What is his average speed for the entire journey in miles per hour ?", "options": [{"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "63", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "In a ∆ABC, two medians AD and BE intersect at G at right angles. If AD = 18 cm and BE = 12 cm, then the length of BD is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "10 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "15 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "20 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "centres-and-medians", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "What is the value of the following expression?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The surface areas of two spheres are in the ratio 25 : 36. What is the ratio of their volumes?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "86.2%", "added": false}, {"text": "88.4%", "added": false}, {"text": "87.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "82.3%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "PQ is a diameter of a circle with centre O. The tangents at R meets PQ produced at A. If ∠ RPQ = 27°, then measure of ∠ RQP is:", "options": [{"text": "63°", "added": false}, {"text": "54°", "added": false}, {"text": "153°", "added": false}, {"text": "27°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Three persons ran for office and got, 1136, 7636 and 11628 votes, respectively. What was the winning candidate's percentage of the total votes?", "options": [{"text": "52%", "added": false}, {"text": "61%", "added": false}, {"text": "59%", "added": false}, {"text": "57%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Two circles touch each other at a point O. AB is a simple common tangent to both the circles touching at point A and point B. If radii of the circles are 9 cm and 4 cm, then find AB.", "options": [{"text": "72 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "144 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "24 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "66", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "Reshma took a loan of ₹12,00,000 with simple interest for as many years as the rate of interest. If she paid ₹9,72,000 as interest at the end of the loan period, what was the rate of interest per annum ?", "options": [{"text": "7.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "8%", "added": false}, {"text": "8.7%", "added": false}, {"text": "9%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "The sides of a cuboid are in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5 and its surface area is equal to the surface area of the cube with side 6 units. What is the approximate volume of the cuboid?", "options": [{"text": "210", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "June, 4", "added": false}, {"text": "June, 3", "added": false}, {"text": "April, 3", "added": false}, {"text": "May, 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}